<title>GERMANY: Bonn sees German 1996 rapeseed crop down one-third.</title>
<headline>Bonn sees German 1996 rapeseed crop down one-third.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's 1996 rapeseed harvest was estimated at two million tonnes compared with 3.1 million tonnes in 1995, the Bonn farm ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry cited winter damage to the crop.</p>
<p>Yields were put at 2.27 tonnes per hectare, versus 3.19 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The ministry stressed the figure was preliminary.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
